cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "nano-agents: Agentic AI from scratch, with a Bayesian lens"
message: "If you use this series in your work or teaching, please cite it as below."
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: "Tran"
    given-names: "Ba-Hien"
abstract: >
  A self-study series and reference codebase building up the foundations of
  agentic AI — bandits, MDPs, RLHF/DPO/GRPO, decoding, tool use, planning,
  retrieval, calibration — from first principles. Every algorithm is derived
  with the math, implemented in <500 lines of NumPy/PyTorch, and accompanied
  by experiments and interactive Jupyter notebooks. The unifying angle is
  probabilistic: decision-making, exploration, retrieval, and reflection
  treated as approximate inference problems.
keywords:
  - reinforcement-learning
  - reinforcement-learning-from-human-feedback
  - bayesian-inference
  - agentic-ai
  - large-language-models
  - rlhf
  - dpo
  - grpo
  - ppo
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/tranbahien/nano-agents"
url: "https://tranbahien.github.io/nano-agents"
date-released: 2026-05-19
